# roadmaps/realtime.md R0: every stretch with interrupts off measured by the
# kernel (TEST_STRETCH), from its entry or a window's end to the next window
# or IRET, with timer channel 0's latched count; the longest, and where, said
# at the end. The shell lists a directory, types a file, reads the game port,
# sounds and faults, so the drivers and the OS server work meanwhile; the
# kernel never keeps interrupts off for half a tick. MAME's AT runs at an
# AT's speed: its numbers are the ones realtime.md records.
program: shell
define: TEST_STRETCH
keys: dir c:\ntype c:\\numbers.txt\njoy\nbeep\ncrash gp\n
timeout: 60
emulators: bochs mame
match: contains
---
rx286: interrupts never off for 10 ms
